kandelo — Licensing
=============================

This project uses a split license model, similar to Linux kernel + musl libc:

  - The platform (kernel, host runtime, SDK, build scripts, examples) is
    licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or later
    (GPL-2.0-or-later). See COPYING for the full text.

  - The runtime library components that are linked into user programs
    (libc/musl-overlay/ and libc/glue/) are licensed under the MIT License.
    See COPYING.runtime for the full text.

This means you can compile and run your own programs — including proprietary
ones — on this platform without the GPL applying to your code. The runtime
library code that gets linked into your program (the syscall glue and libc
overlay) is MIT-licensed, and the kernel communicates with your program via
IPC, not linking.

If you modify the platform itself (kernel, host, SDK), those modifications
are covered by the GPL.


Component Licenses
------------------

GPL-2.0-or-later:
  crates/          Rust kernel and shared types
  host/            TypeScript host runtime
  sdk/             Cross-compilation toolchain wrappers
  scripts/         Build and test scripts
  examples/        Example programs and browser demos

MIT:
  libc/musl-overlay/    Architecture overlay for musl libc (matches musl's license)
  libc/glue/            Syscall glue compiled into user programs

The MIT grant covers the code we wrote in those two directories. They also
hold a few unmodified upstream headers that keep their own licenses; see
"Copied into libc/musl-overlay/ and libc/glue/" below. Each of those licenses
permits linking into proprietary programs, so the paragraph above still holds.


Third-Party Software
--------------------

Third-party code kept in this repository retains its original license. The
list below is the complete inventory; when you add third-party code to the
tree, add it here.

musl libc (libc/musl, git submodule)
  Copyright (c) 2005-2020 Rich Felker, et al. MIT License.
  See libc/musl/COPYRIGHT.

tests/sortix/os-test (git submodule)
  os-test. Copyright Jonas 'Sortie' Termansen and contributors. ISC License.

tests/libc/libc-test (git submodule)
  libc-test from the musl project. Copyright libc-test authors. MIT License.

sdk/rust/libc-upstream (git submodule)
  The Rust libc crate. MIT OR Apache-2.0.

Copied into libc/musl-overlay/ (paths below are relative to it) and
libc/glue/:
  Overlay sources adapted from musl (for example
  src/thread/wasm32posix/pthread_mutex_*.c)
      Keep musl's copyright and MIT License. See libc/musl/COPYRIGHT.
  include/EGL/, include/GLES2/gl2platform.h
      Khronos EGL and OpenGL ES platform headers. Copyright The Khronos
      Group Inc. Apache-2.0 (SPDX tag in each file).
  include/GLES2/gl2.h, include/GLES2/gl2ext.h, include/KHR/khrplatform.h
      Khronos OpenGL ES and KHR headers. Copyright The Khronos Group Inc.
      MIT (license text in each file).
  include/gbm.h
      Mesa libgbm header, mesa-24.3.0. Copyright 2011 Intel Corporation.
      MIT (license text in the file). Provenance in include/gbm.SOURCE.txt.
  include/linux/input-event-codes.h
      Linux UAPI header. Copyright Vojtech Pavlik and Hans de Goede.
      GPL-2.0-only WITH Linux-syscall-note. The syscall note lets user-space
      programs include the header without the GPL applying to them.
  libc/glue/wayland-egl-include/
      wayland-egl headers from the Wayland project. Copyright Kristian
      Høgsberg and Benjamin Franzke. MIT (license text in each file).
  src/setjmp/wasm32/rt.c
      Based on the wasi-libc setjmp/longjmp runtime, which sits in
      wasi-libc's musl tree. MIT (musl's license).

tests/posix/open-posix-testsuite/
  A subset of the Open POSIX Test Suite, taken from the Linux Test Project.
  BSD-2-Clause for newer code, GPL-2.0-or-later for the original suite.
  See tests/posix/open-posix-testsuite/COPYING.

tests/graphics/cts/query-context-cases.inc, surfaceless-case.inc
  Unmodified excerpts from the Khronos VK-GL-CTS dEQP EGL tests. Copyright
  The Android Open Source Project. Apache-2.0. Provenance, hashes and the
  harness adaptations are recorded in tests/graphics/cts/upstream.json.

third_party/stb_truetype.h
  Sean Barrett. MIT or public domain (Unlicense). See third_party/NOTICE.md.

third_party/Inconsolata-Regular.ttf
  Raph Levien and The Inconsolata Project Authors. SIL Open Font License
  1.1. See third_party/NOTICE.md.

packages/registry/wayland-protocols/xml/
  Protocol XML from wayland 1.24.0, wayland-protocols 1.45 and wlroots'
  wlr-protocols. Most files carry their own copyright and MIT-style license
  text; the rest are covered by wayland-protocols' MIT license, copied to
  packages/registry/wayland-protocols/COPYING.

packages/registry/openssl/src/tls/
  TLS 1.2 implementation from WordPress Playground. Copyright WordPress
  Foundation and contributors. GPL-2.0-or-later. Local changes are listed in
  packages/registry/openssl/src/tls/NOTICE.

images/vfs/ruby-todo-app/vendor/
  Rack 3.2.7 (Copyright Leah Neukirchen) and Roda 3.108.0 (Copyright Jeremy
  Evans and contributors), unmodified. MIT License. See MIT-LICENSE in
  vendor/rack/ and vendor/roda/.

programs/sdl2/presets/{image,sound}/tunnelwisp.frag
  "Trailing the Twinkling Tunnelwisp" from Shadertoy
  (https://www.shadertoy.com/view/WfcGWj), ported to GLSL ES 1.00. The
  shader's author marks it CC0. UNRESOLVED: the sound shader's music is
  credited to Pestis, from "Cassini's Cosmic Conclusion"
  (https://github.com/vsariola/cassinis-cosmic-conclusion), whose source has
  no license. No grant from Pestis for reuse of the music has been found.

Packages
  packages/registry/ holds build recipes and patches for third-party
  software (nginx, PHP, MariaDB, Redis, CPython, Git, GNU coreutils, etc.).
  Their sources are fetched at build time and keep their original
  licenses; each package.toml records the license. The exceptions kept in
  this tree are listed above.
